The IAU 2000B nutation routine in crates/xalen-coords (nutation.rs,
nutation_2000b) follows the SOFA routine nut00b in its series layout and in
its treatment of the out-of-phase terms, and
crates/xalen-coords/tests/sofa_reference_crossval.rs uses reference values
taken from the SOFA validation suite (t_sofa_c.c). In respect of that
material this software

  (i)  uses routines and computations derived from software provided by SOFA
       under license; and
  (ii) does not itself constitute software provided by and/or endorsed by
       SOFA.

How it is based upon and differs from the original SOFA software: the code is
written in Rust rather than C or Fortran; nutation_2000b takes Julian
centuries TT from J2000.0 as a single argument instead of a two-part Julian
Date; it returns a NutationResult struct (nutation in longitude and in
obliquity, radians); and it is not an intact copy of any SOFA source file.
No routine name in this project uses the "iau" or "sofa" prefix.

